;; C++'s dg check's effective targets on the reference host (doc/cpp/CPP-SURVEY.md, "As built: CX9 (write-ahead)", review 196's
;; finding 1): what the selectors of g++.dg's dg-error and preprocess files mean on x86_64-alpine-linux-musl with g++ 15.2, read
;; by arbace.repr.cpp.dg before C's table (test/c/dg-targets.edn). Each from gcc 15.2.0's gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp
;; (its proc read, or its probe run with g++ 15.2 on the host: fopenmp's object, musttail's and external_musttail's ,SIBCALL in
;; -fdump-rtl-expand-all, hostedlib's _GLIBCXX_HOSTED 1, the floating types' __STDCPP_*_T__ at -std=c++23, the q and w suffixes
;; compiling). Three are the run's flags' (check-flags), computed by the check: concepts (C++20 on, or -fconcepts), implicit_constexpr
;; (-fimplicit-constexpr), not listed here. A name neither table lists makes the directive undecidable: the file is unsupported
;; with the name in its reason (no longer taken to hold). Read with the Clojure reader.
{:effective {"4byte_wchar_t" true "aarch64_sve" false "bfloat16" true "cxa_atexit" true "default_packed" false
             "exceptions_enabled" true "external_musttail" true "float128" true "float16" true "float64" true "fopenmp" true
             "has_q_floating_suffix" true "has_w_floating_suffix" true "hostedlib" true "ilp32" false "indirect_jumps" true
             "init_priority" true "int32" true "keeps_null_pointer_checks" false "llp64" false "lp64" true "msp430_large" false
             "msp430_small" false "musttail" true "ppc_float128_sw" false "ptr_eq_short" false "short_enums" false
             "short_eq_int" false "size20plus" true "tls" true "wchar" true}}
